IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Criminal Appeal No. 123 of 2021
CITATION: (2021) 4 SCC 675
YEAR: 2021

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.Y. Chandrachud, M.R. Shah

PARTIES:
Alka Khandu Avhad vs Amar Syamprasad Mishra

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Negotiable Instruments Act, 1881

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 138 NI Act, Section 141 NI Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
joint bank account, non-signatory spouse, vicarious criminal liability

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that a joint account holder who is not a signatory to the dishonoured cheque cannot be prosecuted under Section 138 unless vicarious liability applies under Section 141.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 138 NI Act, Section 141 NI Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

